---
description: Rules for Cursor implementation workers in price-memo
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and follow price-memo/AGENTS.md before non-trivial changes. Stay within
the assigned work order and this repository.

- price-memo is a strict unit-price comparison and shopping memo app.
- Preserve exact weight, quantity, and volume semantics. Never promote guessed
  or approximate values to confirmed data.
- Do not add household expense management or AI expense categorization.
- The shared Supabase migration inventory and SQL source of truth are maintained
  in `shared-supabase-db/supabase/migrations/`. Never create, retain, or apply
  migrations from price-memo; never run a database push.
- Do not edit receipt-manager or any other repository from a price-memo worker
  task. If work appears to require another repository, schema change, or
  architectural decision, stop and report the reason and evidence to the
  supervisor.
- Do not silently change public API contracts.
- Prefer small, focused changes and avoid unrelated refactors.
- Run `npm run check` after implementation.
- For browser/UI work, run `npm run devserver:ensure` before Playwright MCP at
  `http://localhost:5273`, then `npm run devserver:stop` when finished. Follow
  AGENTS.md official MCP verification (shared profile at
  `~/.local/state/price-memo/playwright-profile`). Do not kill unrelated port
  occupants or stop reused dev servers from another session. Start 5273 only
  when UI verification needs it; humans use `npm run dev` at
  `http://localhost:5173`.
- Never automate Google OAuth (including clicking app login buttons). Never read
  credentials, cookies, tokens, localStorage, sessionStorage, or profile
  contents. The app login screen alone does not prove Google profile credentials
  are expired; distinguish app-side unauthenticated UI from Google interactive
  re-auth screens.
- When authenticated in-app UI cannot be verified, stop and report exactly:
  `アプリ側は未認証、Google側のログイン状態は未確認`. On Google interactive
  re-auth, stop for manual operator re-login in Playwright MCP. Operator
  observations do not authorize worker OAuth or guarantee future sessions. Do
  not add automatic session recovery; keep unauthenticated vs authenticated MCP
  separation per AGENTS.md.
- For browser/UI work, use Playwright when it materially verifies the task.

At completion, report:
- root cause / implementation intent
- changed files
- verification results
- remaining risks
- anything requiring supervisor review
